       The mmuunnmmaapp() system call deletes the mappings for the specified address
       range,  and  causes further references to addresses within the range to
       generate invalid memory references.  The region is  also  automatically
       unmapped  when  the  process is terminated.  On the other hand, closing
       the file descriptor does not unmap the region.

       The address _a_d_d_r must be a multiple of the page size (but  _l_e_n_g_t_h  need
       not  be).   All  pages containing a part of the indicated range are un‐
       mapped, and subsequent references to these pages will generate SSIIGGSSEEGGVV.
       It is not an error if the indicated range does not contain  any  mapped
       pages.

